---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /about/
title: About the VFL
eyebrow: What this is
lede: A short-season football league for people who work in visual effects! Built around the reality of the job, not despite it.
---
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid" style="gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem); grid-template-columns:1fr">
      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <h2>The idea</h2>
        <p>
          VFX runs on long hours, moving deadlines and contracts that end when the show does.
          Most amateur football leagues assume the opposite: a fixed squad, a nine-month season,
          and a Tuesday that never moves. That combination doesn't survive a client note at 6pm.
        </p>
        <p>
          The VFX Football League is the version that does survive it. A season is
          <strong>eight to eleven games</strong>, roughly one match a week, played on weekday evenings
          between teams from studios across the industry. Short enough that a freelancer can commit to
          the whole thing. Long enough that the table actually means something by the end.
        </p>

        <h2>Who plays</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone working in visual effects, animation or post. Artists and production, but also
          pipeline, R&amp;D, IT, systems, facilities, recruitment, the front desk. Teams are built around
          studios, and the standard is deliberately mixed: some sides are genuinely good, some are
          there for the walk to the pub afterwards, and both get a full season of football.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's open to everyone in the industry regardless of gender, age or ability. If your studio is
          short on numbers, say so, most seasons somebody needs a keeper.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's run</h2>
        <p>
          The league is organised by people who work in the industry, in their own time, and kept as
          cheap as it can be. Costs cover pitches and referees, split between the teams.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything competitive lives on <a href="{{ site.social.sofascore }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sofascore</a>:
          fixtures, results, live standings, form guides and top-scorer charts. That's a deliberate choice.
          It means no one is maintaining a spreadsheet at midnight, results are verifiable, and players get
          a proper profile with their goals on it. This site reads that data live rather than duplicating it.
        </p>

        <h2>The competitions</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid card-grid--3" data-reveal>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__num">Division 1</span>
          <h3>The league</h3>
          <p>{{ honours.competitions[0].blurb }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__num">Division 2</span>
          <h3>The second tier</h3>
          <p>{{ honours.competitions[1].blurb }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__num">VFL Cup</span>
          <h3>The knockout</h3>
          <p>{{ honours.knockouts[0].blurb }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__num">Charity Shield</span>
          <h3>The curtain-raiser</h3>
          <p>{{ honours.knockouts[1].blurb }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Joining</div>
        <h2>How to get a team in</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid card-grid--3">
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 01</span>
        <h3>Find your people</h3>
        <p>Post in your studio's social channel. You need a core of at least eight who'll turn up most weeks. The rest sorts itself out.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 02</span>
        <h3>Message us</h3>
        <p>Send your studio name, a rough headcount and one contact person. We'll tell you when the next season starts and what it costs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 03</span>
        <h3>Turn up</h3>
        <p>You get a fixture list, a spot in the table and a Sofascore page. Everything after that is between you and a 5-a-side pitch.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:2rem" data-reveal>
      <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Enter a team</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/teams/">See who's already playing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
